    "done_when": "One reconciled triage fragment consolidates the four triage batches: the first batch in the plan's evidence record at #triage-first-batch, and the second, third and fourth under docs/evidence/fragments/open-work-is-capped/. It is read from the code at main 5344dcf5.\n\nIt carries:\n- One row per pending reckon plan at that head. Each plan appears exactly once, and the fragment states the count of pending plans the roadmap reports and shows that it equals the row count.\n- Every merge disposition resolved to a final target that is itself kept, following chains to their end and reporting any cycle.\n- The summed keep count against the locked limit of 25.\n\nThe fragment also repairs the row-level findings the four batch reviews recorded, which the plan's section 2 comments list:\n- a section denominator that does not reproduce;\n- counted sections cited without a file and symbol;\n- a head named wrongly;\n- a caption that contradicts its rows.\nEvery counted section in a repaired row names the file and symbol that shows it, checked against the tree at 5344dcf5.\n\nA table sums keep, merge and close per batch and in total, and a figure shows the dispositions. Nothing in any plan is closed or edited. The manifest names the roadmap command and its output count as the row-count evidence.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
